    <string name="always_on_title">Always-on VPN</string>
    <string name="always_on_body">Android can bring GuardWire up automatically after reboot and when the network changes. Enable always-on in system VPN settings and select GuardWire (simplified mode).</string>
    <string name="open_vpn_settings">Open VPN settings</string>

    <string name="about_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="about_guardwire_service">GuardWireVpnService extends VpnService, creates a TUN via VpnService.Builder and shows a foreground notification.</string>
    <string name="about_guardwire_data">IP packets from TUN are wrapped into GuardWire frames and sent over TCP. Frames are encrypted with AES-256-GCM; the key is derived from ephemeral ECDH P-256. Server responses are written back to TUN.</string>
    <string name="about_wireguard">Real mode uses the official WireGuard library: UDP transport, Noise_IK and ChaCha20-Poly1305.</string>
    <string name="about_wireguard_storage">The WireGuard config is stored encrypted in DataStore. The private key is not shown after saving.</string>
    <string name="about_nat">NAT is performed by the server: guardwire-linux-server.py or a WireGuard server. The client only routes packets into TUN and does not do tun2socks.</string>

    <string name="footer">GuardWire/2 · WireGuard · educational project</string>

